Key Responsibilities

Conceive, design, engineer, & implement technology solutions on AEM platform by studying industry best practices;

Conferring with business users;

Studying requirements & processes & investigating problem areas;

Serve as the subject matter expert on AEM specifically & its integrations with various enterprise platforms;

Establish & ensure development & design standards across all AEM development teams on the platform in all areas around AEM & integration with other Adobe Marketing Cloud products &/or Enterprise platforms like – Salesforce CRM, SFMC, API Service Bus, SAML;

Participate & lead technical design discussions & provide detailed estimates to Product owners;

Manage technical delivery of custom development, integrations, & data migration elements of an AEM implementation.

Veolia is looking for a Project Chemist to become part of our Applications Development Center (ADC) team in Ashland, VA. The ideal candidate will deliver laboratory support through both functional and technical contributions, which include conducting chemical and biological testing, performing research in laboratory and field environments, designing and implementing sampling and testing protocols, and applying expertise in chemistry, biology, microbiology, and mathematics within an analytical laboratory environment. The role requires adherence to standard good laboratory practices, QA/QC protocols, and relevant industry standards while collecting and analyzing water, wastewater, and industrial process water samples under various environmental testing conditions.

PRIMARY RESPONSIBILITIES

Responsible for performing basic and instrumental laboratory analyses as associated with water and wastewater treatment;

Perform physical and chemical analyses of water and wastewater samples according to documented requirements and in accordance with established in-house and EPA procedures;

Wet chemistry analyses including colorimetric, titrations, gravimetric, and microbial analysis;

A minimum of 5 years operating ICP and ICP/MS;

Experience with instrumental analyses via UV/VIS, TOC, GC, GC/MS, IC, Lachat Flow Analyzer, and AFS;

Perform, troubleshoot, and maintain proper maintenance and calibration procedures for analytical instrumentation;

Provide analytical support for commercial business groups including sales & marketing and research & development;

Assist in the preparation and writing of technical papers and reports;

Maintain all laboratory operations in accordance with the quality assurance and chemical hygiene plan including maintenance and equipment logs;

Prepare, support, and assist in the writing of technical papers and reports;

Accountable for data quality & timeliness of work;

Adheres to all Veolia Water Tech’s twelve lifesaving rules, EHS safety requirements and procedures.
